  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Find the solutions **in radians** to the equation $2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x+1=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$ Round your answers to **one decimal place**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x+1 & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(-0.5)=-0.463\\,647\u2026\u2248-0.5\n$$\n\nSince $-0.5$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.5$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +(-0.463\\,647\u2026)=2.677\\,945\u2026\u22482.7.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=-0.5$ and $x=2.7.$",
